WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.369
In February 2022,

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.929
the World Journal of Oncology

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:06.329
published an article by a team of 13

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:08.399
researchers claiming that vapers

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.289
are about as likely to get cancer as

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:11.549
people who smoked traditional

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:12.329
cigarets.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.789
Citing this article, Stanton Glantz,

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.589
a tobacco control activist and

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:18.329
retired professor of medicine at the

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.829
University of California, San

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.719
Francisco, claimed that not only

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.279
are there some carcinogens in

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.169
e-cigarette aerosol, but

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:27.329
now there is also direct evidence

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:29.189
that people who use e-cigarettes are

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.469
at increased risk of some cancers.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:32.548
And then the World Journal of

00:00:32.549 --> 00:00:34.379
Oncology's editors retracted

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.209
this study because concerns have

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:37.889
been raised regarding the article's

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.439
methodology source data processing,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.329
including statistical analysis

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.579
and reliability of conclusions.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.079
The editors of the Journal in their

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.609
papers, peer reviewers failed to

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.529
notice the study's many flaws prior

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:51.539
to publication, but they ultimately

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.069
concluded that it was bad enough to

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:54.749
retract. Even so, it's worth

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:56.159
dwelling on the problems because

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.629
they are typical of what we see with

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:59.699
statistical studies on this topic

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.529
and other public policy issues.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.389
The retracted study claimed a large

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:07.319
sample size with data on 154,856

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.339
subjects.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:09.929
For assessing the cancer risk of

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:11.357
vaping versus traditional smoking,

00:01:11.358 --> 00:01:13.229
what we should be looking at

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:14.549
our vapers who never smoked

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:16.079
traditional cigarets and yet have

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.209
cancer. There were 180 vapers

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.219
with cancer in the study, but based

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.139
on general population percentages,

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.089
probably fewer than 100 of them had

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:25.919
never smoked. Traditional cigarets.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.659
That's too small a sample to draw

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:29.279
robust conclusions.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.929
The median age of vapers in the

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:32.759
study was 25 versus

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.249
62 for the traditional smokers,

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:36.359
and they had very different

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.459
breakdowns of income, race, sex

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:39.689
and medical conditions.

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:41.279
Adjusting for all these factors

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.699
would require a minimum of a

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.219
thousand observations.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:45.959
If researchers can query the same

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.669
data sets and arrive at completely

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.469
bizarre results that are as strong

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:50.879
or even stronger than the ones

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.139
they're reporting, they're doing

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:53.369
something wrong.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:54.989
In this case, the authors claimed

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:56.919
active vapers had 2.2 times

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.439
the risk of cancer as the control

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.359
group, but their logistic regression

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:01.829
showed that people who never used

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:03.929
cocaine, heroin or methamphetamines

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:05.789
also had a 2.2 times higher

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.169
risk of getting cancer.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:08.788
Why didn't the authors run with this

00:02:08.789 --> 00:02:09.719
finding?

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.279
That cocaine might be a cancer

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.629
preventative?

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:14.339
Because it's absurd and would likely

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:15.659
have brought ridicule.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:16.969
According to the researchers data,

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.869
being white raises

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:21.239
your cancer risk by 2.6 times.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.099
Having a middle income of between

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.229
25,000 to 65,000

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:27.389
raises your risk 2.3 times.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:28.709
The authors didn't report these

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:30.479
spectacular findings either.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.279
This paper is among the worst of the

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:34.079
anti-vaping articles that managed to

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.849
get published in respectable peer

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:37.409
review journals and cited by

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:39.269
regulators and legislators.

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:40.769
But even the best studies haven't

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:43.049
surmounted a key statistical issue,

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.279
and they tend to distort the

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.509
evidence to make vaping look

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:46.559
dangerous.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.749
An analysis in Internal in Emergency

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.119
Medicine noted 11 flawed studies

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.349
that linked vaping to various

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:53.249
diseases.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:54.689
Some of these studies relied on

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:56.099
surveys that don't report when

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.689
respondents began vaping.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.189
But the Population Assessment of

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:01.169
Tobacco and Health Study reports

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:03.029
age ranges for initiation of

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:04.529
smoking and vaping, as well as

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:05.429
diagnoses.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:07.319
Based on that survey, the authors

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.669
of the Internal in Emergency

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:10.469
Medicine article found that subjects

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:12.419
diagnosed with cancer typically

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.069
started vaping after they were

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:15.719
diagnosed with their conditions.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.849
In fact, just 4% of e-cigarette

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:19.679
users were definitely diagnosed

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:21.179
after they started vaping.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.129
By contrast, about 98%

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:24.929
of smokers were diagnosed after they

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:26.219
started smoking.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.109
Overall, 99% of

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:29.939
cases involve people with a history

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:32.069
of smoking and just 2.3%

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:33.689
of vapers diagnosed with one of the

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:35.189
four health conditions covered by

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:37.019
this study had never been cigaret

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:37.799
smokers.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.599
The tiny population of vapers who

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.459
never smoked traditional cigarets

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:43.199
and who started using e-cigarettes

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.819
before being diagnosed with a health

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:46.749
condition is hard to identify,

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:48.299
unrepresentative of the general

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.279
population and likely too small

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:51.929
to draw conclusions from.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:53.879
No amount of tricky statistical work

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.979
can overcome this basic data issue.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:57.359
There's another problem with the way

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:58.769
the results of these studies are

00:03:58.770 --> 00:03:59.909
reported.

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:01.679
Even if it does turn out that vaping

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.509
has negative health consequences, it

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:05.219
may still be a net positive for

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.899
users who otherwise would go back to

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:08.189
traditional cigarets.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.259
And banning e-cigarettes altogether

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:11.759
would cause some people to turn to

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.319
the black market to get their vaping

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:14.129
fix.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:15.539
Then they would have no idea what

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:16.979
they're sucking into their lungs

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:18.268
because there would be no quality

00:04:18.269 --> 00:04:19.078
control.

00:04:19.079 --> 00:04:21.179
In 2019, underground

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:23.219
manufacturers of marijuana vapes

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:25.049
mixed vitamin E acetate into

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:26.369
their products, which likely

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.559
explains why 2,807

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.449
people ended up hospitalized and

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.789
68 died. Proving that traditional

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:34.649
cigarets cause cancer, which they

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:36.539
do, required two types of

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.789
data; Observational studies

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:40.529
and experimental studies.

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:41.999
First people noticed that cancer

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.319
patients were more likely to be

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:45.479
smokers and non cancer patients,

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:47.219
and then careful experimentation

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.959
teased out some of the mechanisms by

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:50.609
which smoking led to cancer.

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:52.529
Observational studies, even without

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:54.299
data issues, can show only an

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.459
association not causation,

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.169
although most vaping studies claim

00:04:58.170 --> 00:04:59.170
only an association, journailsts,

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:01.799
activists and public officials are

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:03.599
quick to assert causation.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:05.219
Experimental studies can show

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:07.049
causation, but can't measure the

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:08.879
practical extent of an issue or

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.799
possible offsetting factors.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:12.539
One experimental study on vaping

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:13.799
that drew press attention was

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:15.239
published in the Journal of Nuclear

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:17.579
Medicine under the title "Molecular

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.559
Imaging of Pulmonary Inflammation

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:21.149
and Electronic and Combustible

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:23.759
Cigaret Users: a Pilot Study."

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.949
A new study shows e-cigarettes cause

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:27.689
more inflammation in the lungs than

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:29.099
traditional cigarets.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.959
The researchers at the University of

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:33.119
Pennsylvania say vape devices

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:35.039
cause unique damage to the

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:36.569
lungs that is not yet fully

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:37.409
understood.

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:38.879
One problem with this particular

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.769
paper is that it studied only 15

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:41.579
people.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:43.349
Five vapers, five users of

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:45.209
traditional cigarets and five

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.709
people who didn't smoke at all.

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:48.329
However carefully you select groups

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:49.619
of five subjects that can't

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:50.909
represent a broad enough

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:52.679
cross-section of users to draw any

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:54.809
solid conclusions that would require

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:56.399
hundreds of participants.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:57.929
This experiment also relied on

00:05:57.930 --> 00:05:59.549
screening volunteers and made no

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:01.379
attempt at randomness or sampling

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:03.299
the range of population, meaning

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.619
that each of the three groups of

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:06.239
five subjects differed from each

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.889
other in important ways.

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:09.599
The paper did not show that vaping

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:11.489
causes increased lung damage.

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:13.019
In fact, the research didn't check

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:13.859
for that.

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:15.959
Instead, it looked for biomarkers

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:17.129
or chemicals thought to be

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:19.019
associated with lung damage.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:20.309
By that measure, they found no

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:21.899
difference between the five vapers

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:23.459
and the control group of five people

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:25.169
who had never vaped or smoked.

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:26.909
The study did find that uptake of a

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:28.529
chemical thought to react to a

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:30.719
biomarker for lung damage was higher

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:32.099
in the five vapers than in the

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:33.029
control group.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:34.589
But the five cigaret smokers

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:36.149
included in the study had a lower

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:37.469
uptake of that chemical than the

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:39.419
controls, which makes a conclusion

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:41.609
suspect, since we know traditional

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:43.409
cigarets cause lung damage.

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:44.999
Most likely the correlation can be

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.859
attributed to random chance.

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:48.929
And this was a pilot study, meaning

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:50.639
it was aimed not at generating firm

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:52.109
conclusions but in testing

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:53.669
procedures and determining which

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:55.679
hypotheses could be tested

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:57.059
in a subsequent study.

00:06:57.060 --> 00:06:58.649
The authors mention more than 30

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:00.689
statistical tests at the 5% level

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:02.429
of significance, and they may have

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:03.681
conducted more. The 5% significance

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:06.989
level means there's a 5% chance

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:08.489
of getting a positive result by

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:10.499
random chance, even if there is no

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:12.689
association at all in your data.

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:15.179
With 30 tests, you expect 1.5

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:16.589
positive results.

00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:18.479
Even if vaping is unrelated to lung

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:20.429
health. The authors got two positive

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:22.319
results out of 30, which is hardly

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:24.149
strong evidence of anything, and the

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:25.589
two results are among the least

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:27.479
direct in terms of linking vaping to

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.469
lung damage.

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:30.359
The more direct tests of biomarkers

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:31.979
failed to find any differences among

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:32.789
the groups.

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:34.679
A classic prohibitionist argument is

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.359
that while a controversial activity

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:38.309
may not be harmful in itself, it

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:39.749
leads to bad things.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:41.279
In the case of vaping, several

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.079
studies suggest that young vapers

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:44.759
are something like seven times as

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:46.649
likely to smoke traditional cigarets

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:48.239
in the future than similar young

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:49.529
people who don't vape.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:50.879
The data is pretty clear.

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:52.589
So far in the limited studies we

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:53.999
have that it looks like it is a

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.519
gateway for youth smoking.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:58.136
An oft cited paper in this area

00:07:58.137 --> 00:08:00.029
"E-cigarettes and Future

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:01.829
Cigaret Use" is typical of the

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:02.699
genre.

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:05.039
And of 298 Southern California's

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:06.929
17 year old high school students who

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:08.879
didn't vape only 11% were

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.799
smoking cigarets a year later.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:12.899
Among those who were vaping at 17,

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:14.789
40% had taken up old fashioned

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:16.079
cigarets at 18.

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:17.489
The paper did a lot of additional

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:19.139
analysis, but this is the basic

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:20.789
statistic driving the conclusion.

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:22.109
To the authors credit, they were

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:24.299
careful to label this an association

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:26.129
between vaping and future smoking

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:27.509
rather than claiming that vaping

00:08:27.510 --> 00:08:28.709
caused future smoking.

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:30.059
Yet when this paper was cited by

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:31.559
regulatory authorities, they

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:33.298
interpreted it as causal evidence

00:08:33.299 --> 00:08:34.859
and therefore as a justification to

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:35.908
restrict vaping.

00:08:35.909 --> 00:08:37.379
There are reasons to be skeptical

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:38.999
about this kind of research.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.469
Not everyone is honest when they

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:42.509
fill out a survey, especially young

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:44.009
people asked about activities that

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:46.499
are frowned upon, and only 14%

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:47.879
of the students interviewed at age

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.799
17 participated in the follow

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:51.209
up survey a year later.

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:52.439
The missing students may be

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:53.879
systematically different from the

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:55.649
ones recorded in the study.

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:57.509
It's also plausible that teenagers

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:59.249
who vape differ from teenagers who

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:01.319
don't in ways that independently

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:03.179
affect their likelihood of smoking.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:04.829
Perhaps the type of kid who vapes at

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:06.689
17 is more likely to smoke at

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:07.529
18.

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:09.119
In that case, restricting vaping

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:10.919
among 17 year-olds probably won't

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:12.779
reduce smoking at age 18.

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:14.699
In fact, some 17 year-old vapers

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:16.559
will switch to traditional cigarets

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:18.359
or turn to underground purveyors of

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:19.949
e-cigarettes, which would pose a

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:21.749
much more serious health risk.

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:23.309
There's plenty of evidence that many

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:25.229
smokers use vaping to reduce or quit

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:27.419
smoking. In fact, adolescent smoking

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:29.339
has continued to fall as adolescent

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:31.019
vaping has increased.

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:32.879
Another anti-vaping argument is that

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.559
it has negative mental or social

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:36.059
health consequences.

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:37.949
Studies like "Electronic Cigaret

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:39.689
Use and Mental Health," the Canadian

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:41.669
population based study, suffer

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:43.199
from the same issues as studies

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:45.239
linking vaping to future smoking.

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:46.829
It's easy to show that vapers have

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:48.719
more psychological and social issues

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:50.459
than non-vapers, but that's only an

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:51.629
association.

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:53.579
And obvious alternative explanation

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:54.749
is that troubled kids are more

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:56.639
likely to vape either as a form

00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:58.529
of self-medication or because they

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:00.359
have less regard for adult opinion

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:02.159
and rules are perhaps because they

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:03.749
are less supervised or have less to

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:05.909
lose by acting in a diviant way.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.079
Even if we did have good

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:08.819
observational studies suggesting

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:10.889
that vaping is reliably associated

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:12.989
with future smoking, or that vaping

00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:14.639
is associated with mental and health

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:16.559
problems, we would still need

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:18.119
experimental studies to support

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:19.439
causal claims.

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:21.299
Most real experiments are unethical

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:22.859
since participants would have to be

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:24.659
randomly assigned to either vape or

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:26.129
avoid vaping, which is why

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:27.449
researchers look for natural

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:28.499
experiments.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:29.969
A good example of a natural

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:31.589
experiment is intended and

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:33.359
unintended effects of e-cigarette

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:35.339
taxes on youth tobacco use.

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:36.749
The authors used data on youth

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:38.489
smoking and vaping rates in ten

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:40.289
states and two large counties that

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:42.329
enacted e-cigarette taxes between

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:44.759
2010 and 2019.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:45.959
They found that taxes were

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:47.639
associated with a reduction in

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:49.379
vaping among young people, but they

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:50.879
were also associated with an

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:52.289
increase in young people smoking

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:53.819
traditional cigarets.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:55.409
That's good evidence that vaping and

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:57.449
smoking are substitutes. If vaping

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:59.429
led to smoking, a decrease in vaping

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:01.289
would lead to a decrease in smoking.

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:02.819
Several other natural experiment

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:04.589
studies reinforce the idea that

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:06.599
vaping and smoking are substitutes,

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.069
although the rate of substitution

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:09.119
seems to vary in different

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:10.169
populations.

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:11.579
But we still have a lot to learn in

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:13.109
this area. The evidence to date

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:14.909
suggests that discouraging vaping

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:16.469
will lead to increased smoking and

00:11:16.470 --> 00:11:18.419
very likely worse public health.

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:20.189
This research suggests that the 15

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:22.139
to 20% e-cigarette tax,

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:23.699
which was part of the original Build

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:25.679
Back better act that was eventually

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:27.149
taken out, probably would have

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:29.489
reduced youth vaping by about 3%

00:11:29.490 --> 00:11:31.109
and increase youth smoking by about

00:11:31.110 --> 00:11:31.889
2%.

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:33.449
Given the evidence that vaping is

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:35.369
far less hazardous than smoking,

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:37.379
more teen-smoking instead of vaping

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:39.089
doesn't represent an improvement in

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:40.049
public health.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:41.579
None of this research shows that

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:43.379
vaping is safe and it doesn't rule

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:44.849
out the possibility of negative

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:45.989
health effects that haven't been

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:47.909
found yet. But in public policy,

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:49.529
the most important question is

00:11:49.530 --> 00:11:51.029
instead of what?

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:52.709
In real life there are no solutions,

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:53.909
only trade offs.

00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:55.679
There's overwhelming evidence that

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:57.449
the alternative to vaping is cigaret

00:11:57.450 --> 00:11:59.519
smoking. Vaping represents a huge

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:01.019
improvement for public health.

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:02.759
Government officials generally fail

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:04.319
to reason in these terms.

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:06.389
They tax, ban, and regulate

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:08.009
as if their policies exist in a

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:10.109
vacuum, setting statistically

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:11.669
dubious studies to support their

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:12.990
preconceived policies.

